The impedance of the tube transducer was measured using an electrical
impedance analyser (4294A, Keysight Technologies, CA, USA). The spectrum
is shown in @fig:Ze_spectrum where the resonance of the
fundamental radial mode is apparent at
$16.79 med upright("k") upright("Hz")$. This mode was targeted for
generating an axially focused field for high intensity cavitation. The
tube transducer was therefore excited by a sinusoidal voltage signal at
this frequency for all results presented. Amplification and impedance
matching are described in section~@sec:methods_tube_excitation, below. A
second resonance frequency appearing at
$55.89 med upright("k") upright("Hz")$ is the first axial mode, but the
pressure field generated inside the tube bore at this frequency does not
have the desired distribution and so was not applied in this study.

#figure(image("source/fig2_impedance_matching.png"),
